comp.graphics	re computer graphics to vcr getting an image from a computer monitor to a videotape is harder than it looks the standard vga and ega outputs are very different than the ntsc format used by televisions while there is equipment that will do the conversion it is hard to get your hands on and costs quite a bit if you have access to an amiga computer that has an ntsc output you can transfer certain types of graphic files by modem and tape them from the ntsc output unfortunately this would be frame by frame and would lead to unbelievably scratchy animation unless you had a good amiga animation program otherwise see if your local public access cable station has equipment that you can use
