comp.os.ms-windows.misc	re workgroup questions conven ram and licensing in article ra abh h eosvcr wimsey bc ca aew eosvcr wimsey bc ca alan walford writes i would be very appreciative if someone would answer a few questions about windows for workgroups i currently have novell netware lite which does not work with windows very well and is a conventional memory hog ver i am considering moving all our machines to w wg q how much conventional ram does w wg use over and above the driver for the network card about kbyte without novell support q if i have a novell ne card are the lsl and ipx drivers still needed no q does w wg do a license check over the network to ensure each machine is running its own licenced copy of w wg note i do not want to break the license agreement and i will buy a copy of w wg for each of our machines it is just that i would like to try it out first to see if it meets our needs returning one opened copy is much easier than returning n opened copies no q if you buy the upgrade to windows for w wg does it replace all of win as you install it or does it depend on current win files nearly all q if i install windows nt on my server when it comes out will i have any troubles with the w wg machines we run mixed wnt beta and w wg no problem apart from printer sharing beta problem when i started this message i was going to ask only questions but i got carried away i ll stop now we had problems with mouse drivers using w wg where windows didn t seems to be more critical about it it was actualy a port problem with the network card running on x e we changed it to x now everything is allright i think it has to do with the ami bios as well i look forward to your replies al alan walford eos systems inc vancouver b c canada tel aew eosvcr wimsey bc ca or uunet wimsey bc ca eosvcr aew ralf rutherford telecom aust mhsnet rruther cssc melb tansu com au network services snail blackburn rd clayton vic customised software solutions australia center melbourne phone fax
