h other xga cards so multiple desktops like on the mac may not be far away since this is an architecture its resolution and color depth isn t fixed ibm implements only bit color while other companies can have bit color through ibm technical licenses refresh rates up to hz ensures flicker free rock solid images to reduce visual discomfort and is vga compatible up to x on os some monitor types usable by mac see mac section above for specific details expansion both mac ibm scsi only external device expansion interface common to both mac and ibm allows the use of any device hard drive printer scanner nubus card expansion mac plus only some monitors and cd rom main problem there are a lot of external devices which are internal terminated which causes problems for more then two devises off the scsi port a scsi chain is supposed to be terminated only at the begining and at the end any other set up causes problems for either mac or ibm scsi devices per scsi controller bit asynchronous mb s ave and synchronous mb s max transfers difference is due to scsi software drivers fast scsi is a misname for bit scsi in scsi mode see scsi for details scsi devices per scsi controller in scsi mode scsi is fully scsi compliant and bit scsi tends to be implemented as a very fast scsi since it does not require the different controller interfaces in hardware and software that and bit scsi do transfer speeds are mb s with mb s burst bit mb s with mb s burst bit and mb s with mb s burst bit wide and fast since bit scsi can use scsi software drivers and hardware at bit scsi speeds and as such is limited to devices sometimes it is mistakenly called fast scsi bit fast scsi requires a scsi software driver and scsi electronics but can still use the scsi ports wide bit and bit scsi require a different scsi port electronics and software driver from scsi which makes them more expensive than other scsi interfaces mac scsi asynchronous scsi built in standard since the plus even though apple developed some specifications for scsi controlers the os scsi manager needs to be rewritten to take full advantage of the features of both scsi interfaces as a result present scsi macs use bit scsi as a fast asynchronous scsi presently quadras are the only macs with a scsi controller chip built in digital review oct v n p though they lack some other parts of the hardware like the wide scsi port interface since other macs require a nubus card to use scsi older nubus macs had a bottleneck due to the speed of the nubus and cpu rumor some cyclone macs june will come with a wide fast scsi port standard and have a rewritten os scsi manager ibm scsi scsi is not too wide spread yet generally not bundled with systems except as add on eisa and vesa local bus adapters avalable like the mac bit scsi is used as a very fast scsi by most controllers out there unlike the mac ibm has no exact scsi controller specifications which results in added incompatibilities for scsi mac memory expansion with a few exceptions the mac has used non parity pin bit simm memory expansion since the plus while pin bit parity simms could be used in these macs only special iicis could make use of the parity feature by convension both simm types are called pin simms the iifx used pin parity simms the lc iii c and q all use a new pin simm that is accessable by bits at a time and is used in ibms the mac does a complete memory check at startup by writing reading every memory location if something is seriously wrong with a simm the mac will not boot and give a sound chord indicating what the problem is since macs made before feb managed memory baced on data path simms had to be installed in pairs bit or in sets of bit the centris and quadra eliminate this with a new memory management setup that allows memory to be upgraded one simm at a time if the simms are the same size are used then the memory is interleaved across the two simms resulting in a performance boost on ram access macworld apr printers adbs and modems built in interfaces standard monitor interface and sound input built in on most present macs pds available in se all present non powerbook macs bit se portable lc lc ii classic line and bit operates at cpu s mhz maximum through put data path in bytes cpu s mhz q c mhz mb s q q mhz mb s standardized with the lc and bus designs with an adapter one nubus card can be used in iisi and c problem some cards have timing dependency which slows through put down nubus mac ii bit mhz bus clock to transaction bus cycle ratio and contiguous hand shake transactions at mb s theoretical peak mb s built in on all modular macs except the lc series c and performa the se could be adapted to use this and there was even a mac plus scsi nubus supports every possible expansion from cpu to ethernet to dma nubus nubus mac ii back compatable mhz bus clock avg throughput mb s burst mode mb s future card designs will be instead of the old quickring a peer to peer bus used in parallel with nubus apple s vlbus architecture is identical to that of vlbus byte burst mode mb s byte in development cpu expansion handled either through the pds or the nubus unlike pds nubus cpu cards example radius rocket allow use of multiple processors at the same time this is like having two or more macs in the same box able to dual task or joinly process depending on the card or software involved each nubus card needs its own memory but most nubus cards of this type come with mb ram simms on the card standard ibm memory expansion parity simms non parity simms some newer models do a mac like simm memory check or a dozen or so different types of memory boards hd interfaces limited to hard drives by design or lack of development mfm modified frequency modulation rll run length limited only used with smaller mb hard drives ide integrated device electronics asynchronous mb s max and synchronous mb s max transfer currently the most common standard and is mainly used for medium sized drives can have more than one hard drive esdi enhanced small device interface mb s throughput generally considered better interface than scsi in many ways but not common enough for practical consideration outside of hard drives device choices are very limited compared to scsi bus interfaces new plug and play isa and eisa compatable cards may have problems working with old cards infoworld pc week vaporware isa bit interfaces common has bit data path limit which produces a mb limit for which there are software workarounds pc mag mb s byte uses edge triggered interrupts can t share them hence comes the irq conflict limited busmastering capabilities some cards aren t bandwidth limited com ports lpt ports game ports midi card etc while others are video and disk controllers dominant factor but it s showing its age most isa motherboard designs are bit pc world feb mca micro channel ibm s and bit bus allows use of more than one cpu in a computer dct and anything can talk to anything as fast as the two components involved can handle it never took off because it was incompatible with isa and eisa planned to be bus interface of ibm powerpc carl jabido eisa nubus mac ii is closest mac equivalent bit mhz burst mode mb s it also has the ability to self configure cards like mca and allows multiple bus masters sharable interrupt and dma channels and multiple cpu use vesa local bus vlb sometimes mistakenly refereed to as pds local bus standard runs at cpu clock rate burst modes mb s bit mb s bit byte limited to three slots but allows bus mastering and will coexist with either isa or eisa consitered ideal for video and disk i o dell has filled a claim that this violates one of their patents mel martinez quickring apple s faster mb s burst version of vlb architecture byte might show up in some ibm and powerpc machines byte in development pci intel s version of local bus that is intended to totally replace isa eisa mca in development oses assumes full installation print drivers fonts multifinder etc and multiple application use m