rec.autos	re dumbest automotive concepts of all time no reverse lights are to warn others that you are backing up they aren t bright enough to typically see by without the brake and tail lights craig perhaps instead of this silly argument about what backup lights are for couldn t we agree that they serve the dual purpose of letting people behind your car know that you have it in reverse and that they can also light up the area behind your car while you re backing up so you can see backup lamps on current models are much brighter than they used to be on older cars those on my taurus wagon are quite bright enough to illuminate a good area behind the car and they re much brighter than those on my earlier cars from the s and s insofar as vettes having side backup lights look at a or model or perhaps a year or two earlier too and you ll see red side marker lamps and white side marker lamps both near the car s hindquarters those aren t just white reflectors harv
rec.autos	re station wagons was open letter to nissan in article apr leland stanford edu tedebear leland stanford edu theodore chen writes but you ll never catch me dead in a minivan even a minivan based on viper running gear hmmmm not sure since no such beast exists i can tell you another though you won t catch me dead in a gmc syclone or typhoon either bhp or not not even the fact that clint eastwood has one just my taste no rational reasons for it teddy p s i think the audi s gets a liter v next year car just tested the s wagon with banger and speed manual rave review except for servotronic audi is trying to recoup the development costs for the v and since the v is not selling well they are sticking it into the series cars neat marketing trick eh yeah a v v wouldn t be a bad idea as competition for the upcoming bimmer i would it maybe they can use a liter version to avoid conflicts with the v model then strip off all the luxo garbage let the s remain with the flared arches and fat tires to go fight with the m maybe turn up the boost a wee bit to bump bhp up to say or so while keeping the v with mercedes e style subtlety blah blah blah eliot
