rec.motorcycles	need advice for riding with someone on pillion i need some advice on having someone ride pillion with me on my ninja this will be the the first time i ve taken anyone for an extended ride read farther than around the block we ll be riding some twisty fairly bumpy roads the mines road mt hamilton loop for you sf bay areans this person is lbs and fairly small so i don t see weight as too much of a problem but what sort of of advice should i give her before we go i want her to hold onto me rather than the grab rail out back and i ve heard that she should look over my shoulder in the direction we re turning so she leans with me but what else are there traditional signals for slow down or go faster or i hafta go pee etc i really want this to be a positive experience for us both mainly so that she ll want to go with me again so any help will be appreciated thanks bob bob wert rmw genie gene com rwert well sf ca us dod ama ninja r mustang lx seven turns on the highway seven rivers to cross sometimes you feel like you can fly away sometimes you get lost
