sci.electronics	re subliminal message flashing on tv in article hpfcso fc hp com myers hpfcso fc hp com bob myers writes hi i was doing research on subliminal suggestion for a psychology paper and i read that one researcher flashed hidden messages on the tv screen at ths of a second is that possible i thought the maximum rate the tv was even capable of displaying images was th of a second or th of a second for an image composed of only odd or even scan lines you are correct the fastest complete image that could be presented on tv would be one field which is of a second approximately of course the phrase tv screen is often thrown around in reference to any crt display so perhaps this researcher wasn t using normal tv rates might even be a vector strokewriter display in which case the lower limit on image time is anyone s guess and is probably phosphor persistence limited actually a lot of this work used to be done with a crt that had a beamsplitter mounted in front and a tachistoscope driving it the tachistoscope is really just a slide projector with a very fast shutter low tech but it does the job scott
