tions more liberal ones are willing to make allowances for situations where a literal interpretation would lead to painful results it is noted that at the time it was possible for a man to divorce his wife almost on a whim thus a common explanation in the more liberal approach is that jesus was trying to protect people from this sort of thing not to establish an absolute rule to which there could never be exceptions catholics as is typical with catholic ethics take a theoretical hard line but allow for exceptions in practice through the process of anullment in the last discussion most of our non catholic readers seemed to accept with some reluctance that in some cases there might be no good alternative but there was a feeling that the church should often be doing a better job of helping people prepare for marriage and deal with problems that come up during it and that in a properly run church divorce should not be necessary clh
