 clearly behind firearms the protection factor does not strongly outweigh the mindless mayhem factor given society as we now experience it it seems safer to get rid of as many guns as possible that may be an error but enough active voters believe in that course this is exactly why law should be based on reasoned thought not immediate perception of course it doesn t always work that way fortunately while there are no guarantees logic sometimes does prevail and if not there are still means for correction as far as enough active voters are concerned that is still an open question until the vote is made how do you intend to silence rkba supporters talk all you want talk about the good old days when you used to own firearms after a while such talk will take on the character of war stories and no one will be very interested anymore you portray a possible scenario for the future but how will you silence rkba supporters right now as long as public debate is allowed such debate will continue if we allow public debate to be restricted or denied then we will get a gov t we deserve al standard disclaimer
