els at which people react to what they see at the most fundamental level you do not have to consciously recognize the racial element you simply tend to empathize more with people who are like yourself as far preferring christian over moslem i am an atheist myself and i think you ll agree that in the us the majority of people do not typically discriminate on the basis of religion nor give it a particularly important place in their world view dave
